ean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-two-thirds-band"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-two-thirds-band"],"id":"long.thm-two-thirds-band","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.48 (Two-thirds band: exact localisation of post-take skip-unsafety)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.48, p. 57, label thm:two-thirds-band","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Write a positive residual as $1/R$. A skipped rank $k$ passes the sufficient dyadic test precisely when $R\\ge2^k$. Suppose a weight at rank $b$ is taken without exhausting the residual: with $q=2^b-1$, assume $0<R<q$. The new reciprocal residual is $Rq/(q-R)$. If the next take is at rank $c\\ge b+2$, put $m=2^{c-1}$. The last skipped rank is dyadically unsafe exactly when\n$$\nm-1<\\frac{Rq}{q-R}<m,\n \\quad\\text{equivalently}\\quad\n \\frac{q(m-1)}{q+m-1}<R<\\frac{qm}{q+m}.\n$$\nClearing the positive denominators proves the equivalence. The interval has width $q^2/((q+m)(q+m-1))$.*\n\n*For a single skipped rank, $c=b+2$ and $m=2q+2$. The width is then $q^2/((3q+1)(3q+2))<1/9$, and the interval lies inside $2q<3R<2q+2/3$. In this single-skip case, the cited corollaries exclude integral $R$ and show that a reduced pre-take residual $p/(2D)$ with $p,D,q$ odd can be unsafe only if $p\\ge7$. The latter conclusion uses the divisibility by $4$ of $6D-2pq$ under the unsafe-band inequalities.*\n\n*These are local transition statements, not bounds on the actual half-greedy orbit. Dyadic safety is only sufficient for the current tail test. The odd-coprime data $(p,D,b)=(17,41,3)$ give an unsafe single-skip example; no conclusion that the half-greedy orbit avoids such data follows from the band calculation.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-two-thirds-band","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-two-thirds-band","id":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.thm-two-thirds-band%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_two_thirds_band%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/edges/%5B%22long.thm-two-thirds-band%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_two_thirds_band%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_two_thirds_band"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-two-thirds-band","id":"field:06ae220ae45c48ad1c37a3c853acf1100ca2e53d415eec0b7609b9b24f811876","kind":"citation_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-two-thirds-band","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"citation_ids","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/citations/cite.long.thm-two-thirds-band"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/evidence/mapping.long.thm-two-thirds-band","id":"field:3d494a769f6248afbf59e3722affe8b21fb044fe5fea090717f61afff8e0baab","kind":"subject_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/evidence/mapping.long.thm-two-thirds-band","semantic_class":"provenance_field_reference","source_field":"subject_ids","to":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-two-thirds-band"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:57133a32273c39019ea3f4ba3de79281b7177858848a9345731e250a68a8c176/nodes/long.thm-two-thirds-band","id":"f